# Site-wide security headers.
#
# Referrer-Policy is the important one: share tokens travel in the URL query
# (?t=, ?deck=<id>&token=, ?collection=<uuid>&token=). strict-origin-when-cross-
# origin stops the full URL (with token) from leaking in the Referer header to
# third parties on outbound navigations (TCGPlayer affiliate links, the YouTube
# embed, the QR image service). frame-ancestors/X-Frame-Options stop the
# authenticated, mutating UI from being clickjacked inside a hostile iframe.
#
# NOTE: a full script-restricting Content-Security-Policy is deliberately NOT
# set here — the app is a single no-build Index.html with inline module scripts
# and inline styles, so a real script-src would need 'unsafe-inline' (defeating
# the point) or build-step nonces. Tracked as a follow-up. frame-ancestors is
# safe to ship standalone (it only restricts framing, not script execution).
/*
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains

# Long-cache + permissive CORS on proxied Lorcast art.
#
# Lorcast (cards.lorcast.io) sends no Cache-Control header, so without an
# override Netlify edge treats the response as uncacheable — every miss
# forwards to Lorcast and pulls bandwidth across both legs of the proxy.
# A 30-day immutable cache lets Netlify's CDN absorb almost the entire
# load: each edge POP fetches once, then serves locally for a month.
# Image URLs are content-addressed (Lorcast appends a hash query param when
# they re-publish), so a long cache won't trap stale art — a new card
# revision arrives at a new URL the catalog ETL picks up.
#
# Access-Control-Allow-Origin: * guarantees canvas exports (deck poster,
# card poster, mover-tile) stay untainted no matter what Lorcast does with
# their CORS headers later. The browser only enforces CORS on
# crossOrigin="anonymous" <img>s — same-origin requests ignore it — but
# pinning ACAO is free insurance.
/img-proxy/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000, immutable
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
